WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:00.763
Welcome.

2
00:00:00.763 --> 00:00:04.056
This is the executive
briefing for Book 06 of the

3
00:00:04.056 --> 00:00:07.762
Federal Modernization
Workbook, SQL Server identity.

4
00:00:07.762 --> 00:00:11.416
It's for the people who make
the calls: the CIO, the CISO,

5
00:00:11.416 --> 00:00:15.401
the data platform owner,
application owners and sponsors.

6
00:00:15.401 --> 00:00:16.825
The argument is short.

7
00:00:16.825 --> 00:00:21.042
Every domain-joined SQL Server
inherited Windows Authentication,

8
00:00:21.042 --> 00:00:26.087
and none of it is visible to the identity
plane that enforces multifactor sign-in.

9
00:00:26.087 --> 00:00:30.175
The estate has to be counted and
shrunk before any login moves.

10
00:00:30.175 --> 00:00:34.297
And the destination is an Entra
token on every connection,

11
00:00:34.297 --> 00:00:38.162
finished well before the
program's own NTLM block date.

12
00:00:38.162 --> 00:00:42.538
Each decision slide names the decision,
its owner and when it's needed.

13
00:00:42.538 --> 00:00:45.600
Let's start with why the
database is where this hides.
